sample_frames.py: Takes videos from data/dr_videos and samples 7 frames to data/informative_frames/frames_raw_extract

grade_frames.py: Take frames from data/frames_raw_extract and grade into 2 (or 3) classes using an interface.
At the moment only the 2 class setting is used.

crop_frames.py: Use the 5 trained cropping models to crop the extracted frames (data/informative_frames/frames_raw_extract)
and move them to 0 and 1 folders in data/informative_frames/frames_cropped

classify_frames.py: Use images in data/informative_frames/frames_cropped to train 5 EfficientNets for classifying frames
into informative and not with 5 splits. Models are saved in models. The split_info_5fold_{timestamp}.csv that saves the
mapping seems to be lost unfortunately

extract_inf_frames.py: Use trained cropping model ensemble and trained informative frames model ensemble to both crop
and filter all videos in data/dr_videos;
results are saved in ensemble_results (at the moment, needs to be moved to data) and contains the clips and txts/plots
that visualize the confidences for each frame

split_info_full.csv contains the annotations for all of the 7x417=2919 frames (also an train/val column that can be removed)

